'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 8''' was the eighth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on August 12, 2026 at the Tokuyama Municipal Gymnasium in [[Tokuyama]]. The show was the first NOPW event after the [[Island Invasion Tour 2026|Island Invasion]] in [[Fangatapu]], [[Vaiahi]], and the first of the two G1 fall-out shows, headlined by [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]] defeating [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] in the main event and closing with [[Leoni Masua]]'s announcement that he would enter the [[G1 Climax 2026]].

The show is best remembered for the silence: [[Marcus Vance]], three days removed from losing the [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]] to [[Jusuf Muntasir]] at Island Invasion, walked to the ring with no music and no entrance, said nothing, defeated [[Mamadou Diallo]], and walked out. The clip became the most shared in NOPW Wednesday history — a record broken one week later.

== Background ==

The [[Island Invasion Tour 2026|Island Invasion]] on August 9 — Leoni Masua's homecoming — reshaped NOPW: three championship changes ([[Jusuf Muntasir]] took the Intercontinental Championship from Vance, [[Diego Reyes]] and [[Haruto Kimura]] took the [[IGO Tag Team Championship]] from the Usos, and [[Yuto Ono]] took the [[World Television Championship]] from [[Jin Tanaka]]), a clean loss for [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] to [[Taumafa Vaiahi|Taumafa]], a non-title win for Leoni over KAZUKI, and the public collapse of the [[Cannon Club]] — [[Big Stan]] and Diallo walked out on Kengo backstage, and [[Malo Vaiahi|Malo]] left the faction's orbit entirely.

Key storylines entering Episode 8:
* The Cannon Club held one title (the [[IGO Junior Tag Team Championship]] and nothing else after Island Invasion's three losses) and had no leader the locker room believed in. Kengo needed a win in the worst way.
* Vance had lost his faction, his title, and — apparently — his voice. His first appearance since the Jusuf defeat was the show's central question.
* Jusuf, the new Intercontinental Champion, defended the title for the first time.
* The G1 Climax 2026 field was days from announcement, and the champion's participation was the open secret of the week.

