== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' The Seigigun young lions opened the show — Iwata's cutter finishing Yamamoto at 9:47 after a clean, competitive contest between stablemates. '''Crowd:''' warm opener POP. '''IWATA''' chants on the finish.
* '''Match 2:''' Malo's singles run, now fully out of the Cannon Club's orbit, ran through the fallen television champion — Tanaka's brawling had its moments, but Malo's power told. '''Crowd:''' '''MALO''' chants. HEAT for Tanaka's shortcuts.
* '''Match 3:''' Jusuf's first Intercontinental defense. Morita, the company man, took the match on a day's notice and took everything Jusuf had — the mosaraza kneebar at 6:12, and when Morita would not tap, the referee stopped it. Jusuf left without acknowledgment. '''Crowd:''' uneasy silence through the match. HEAT for the walk-out. Respect applause for Morita.
* '''Match 4:''' The tag title rematch — the Usos' contractual return match, four days after losing the titles. The champions' first defense: Reyes' explosiveness and Kimura's speed against the twins' timing, which had won them two years of gold. The Cobra Clutch on Riku set up the pin at 15:40. The Usos' rebuild starts at zero. '''Crowd:''' '''COBRA''' chants. HEAT for the Usos' frustration — Tama took the mic and blamed Kengo by name.
* '''Match 5:''' The silence. Vance walked through the crowd entrance aisle with no music, no pose, no acknowledgment of anything — the building went quiet on its own. He chopped the Cannon Club's wall down by the knee, exactly as he would later do to Taumafa in the G1 Final, and finished Diallo with the Drill Driver at 12:33. He said nothing before and nothing after. '''Crowd:''' '''VANCE''' chants — the babyface turn is total. The clip passed Episode 7's Cannon Club attack within 24 hours.
* '''Match 6:''' The main event — KAZUKI against Kengo, the faction-breaker against the man whose faction had broken on its own. Kengo's shortcuts (the eye rake, the exposed turnbuckle) kept it close; the Twin Star Press at 18:05 was clean and undeniable. Kengo's second straight singles loss since Island Invasion. '''Crowd:''' '''KAZUKI''' chants. NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo. Post-match: Jusuf walked to the ring with the Intercontinental Championship, held it up at Vance on the floor, and said nothing either. Vance stared through him and left. '''Crowd:''' stunned, then a slow '''VANCE''' swell.

== Main event segment: The Chief goes to war ==

The show closed with the IGO Heavyweight Champion. Leoni Masua walked out with the championship and the namo, stood center ring, and ended a week of speculation:

''"The Chief does not wait for challengers. The Chief goes to war. I am entering the G1."''

The last champion to enter the G1 did so in 2019. The announcement made official what the block draw would confirm one week later: the champion's road to [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]] runs through the tournament itself.

'''Crowd:''' deafening '''LEONI''' chants. MEGA POP for the announcement line.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The silence begins.''' Vance's walk — no music, no entrance, no words — became the defining image of the G1 season. He would not speak again until October 18.
* '''Kengo's freefall.''' Two straight losses, a faction in open revolt, and the Usos blaming him on live television. The block draw one week later would place him in Block A with Leoni, Vance, and Big Stan — the man he betrayed and the men who left him.
* '''Jusuf holds the gold.''' The Intercontinental Champion's first defense ended in a stoppage, as all of them do. Nobody taps to Jusuf; the referee saves them.
* '''The G1 is coming.''' The field and block draw were announced at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 9|Episode 9]] on August 19.

